# A NAME THAT A STATEMENT DEFINES ON A PROTOTYPE UNDER A KEY THAT NOBODY KNOWS AT BUILD TIME, AND A LOOKUP THAT IS SAID TO FIND NOTHING. Link keeps a row without a key for such a prototype, and the walk refused
# every "finds nothing" above the objects of that class and of its heirs, whatever the name. Where the answer rests on the guard of the asked name anyway (the objects may get another prototype), the guard answers for the unknown key too:
# the record has no row for it, so a name that lies on the prototype when the guards begin differs from the record and ends its guards, and a later definition ends them as every write does.
